`priv_size()` is called here and the family descriptor was validated to have it.
The `max(...,1)` means a zero-size priv still gets a container, fine, but the
overflow checking below is heavier than needed: the only unbounded term is the
family-provided size, so one `check_add_overflow` per family is sufficient, and
`kvzalloc()` would reject anything near `SIZE_MAX` anyway.  Two nested overflow
checks plus the 'overflow' label add ~10 lines for a case no in-tree family can
hit.  Also: the container base ends up at `priv_offset` - `offsetof(priv)`, whose
alignment relies on `offsetof(priv)` being a multiple of `SMP_CACHE_BYTES`; add a
`static_assert(offsetof(struct ctlv_priv_container, priv) == CTLV_PRIV_ALIGN)` or
similar to document the invariant.

