Teardown order: after `ctlv_device_fini()` the family pointer is cleared and
bindings nulled without any lock for the ops[] writes (the loop at the end writes
`ctlvdev->ops[index].binding`/priv with no lock).  Readers (`ctlv_op_find` users in
introspection/event paths) are excluded by the registration write lock having
been taken above, but not ones that run without it (`ctlv_event_create` from an
async family worker calling `ctlv_op_find`, which reads ->schema only, OK).  It
works, but the reasoning is spread over three files; please add a comment listing
who may still read ops[] at this point.

Also two back-to-back scoped write-lock sections plus fini in between could be
one if fini did not need the lock free; the comment explains why.  Fine.

