`subsys_initcall` with a tristate module compiles to `module_init`, so the choice is
harmless but suggests built-in ordering; a plain `module_init()` would be more
honest.  Also note `ctlv_module_init` has a single failure label; the goto adds
nothing over an inline unregister.

