Summary of the most serious issues:

- Commit message omits most of what the patch does (chardev, uevent, stub fill, op state API) and the series is not bisect-buildable before this patch: patches 5-11 add .c files that are not compiled until the Makefile hunk here.
- `registration_lock` (rwsem, read side) is held across `copy_from_user()` and the whole op callback, so a stalled user copy blocks `ctlv_destroy()` and, via writer-pending, every new open/ioctl.
- Output buffers are kvmalloc'd unzeroed and copied to userspace (reply and error info); safe only if every builder path writes every byte. Prefer kvzalloc.
- chardev lacks `stream_open()`/`no_llseek` although read ignores the offset.
- Dead/redundant code: unreachable !child in `chain_check`, empty `ctlv_file_open_pinned()`, redundant @owner param, default arm in `ctlv_op_check_mode`, add/del wrappers, empty root-family stub hooks.
- `ctlv_create()` duplicates `release()` logic in `err_free`; family claim is spent after minor allocation and persists on failure.
- Exported provide/`state_set` and the `CTLV_OP_*` macros lack kernel-doc.
